<title>UK: Pillar, SITQ sell N.Irish shopping centre.</title>
<headline>Pillar, SITQ sell N.Irish shopping centre.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-01-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Britain's Pillar Property Investments Plc said it had sold a shopping centre jointly owned with its venture partner SITQ Immobilier of Canada for 13.5 million stg.</p>
<p>In a statement, the company said it had exchanged contracts to dispose of the Fairhill Shopping Centre in Ballymena, Northern Ireland to a local charitable trust.</p>
<p>&quot;The price represents an initial yield of 7.25 percent and an equivalent yield of 8.6 percent,&quot; it added.</p>
<p>Pillar said the funds from the disposal would be reinvested into further shopping centre investments.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
